{"term":"tippelzone","lang":"nl","script":"latin","romanization":null,"category":"sex_work_pornography","subcategory":"street_prostitution","concept":"street_prostitution","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":20,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":2000,"regional":null,"definition":"A municipality-designated zone where street prostitution is legally tolerated and regulated, equipped with safety infrastructure such as lighting, safe-sex facilities, and supervisory services.","english_term":"prostitution tolerance zone","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Distinctively Dutch policy instrument; several cities including Utrecht, Rotterdam, and Eindhoven operated tippelzones in the 1990s–2000s; most have since closed following policy shifts; the concept is translatable but the institutionalized Dutch form is culturally specific."}
